Track the minimum, maximum and sum in one pass. Subtract the minimum and maximum from the sum, then divide by `n - 2`. The sum can reach about 100 × 10^6 = 10^8, which fits in an `int`, but I use `long` to be safe.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public double Average(int[] salary) {
        long sum = 0;
        int min = int.MaxValue, max = int.MinValue;
        foreach (int s in salary) {
            sum += s;
            if (s < min) min = s;
            if (s > max) max = s;
        }
        return (double)(sum - min - max) / (salary.Length - 2);
    }
}
```

