traces.inference_trace:
The answer is the sum of the prime factors of `n`, counted with multiplicity.

Reaching a multiple of the current length takes one Copy All and then (k−1) Pastes, which is k operations for a factor k. Splitting a composite factor into its prime factors never costs more, since a·b ≥ a+b for a, b ≥ 2. So the minimum is the sum of the prime factors, and `n = 1` gives 0.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int MinSteps(int n) {
        int res = 0;
        for (int d = 2; d <= n; d++) {
            while (n % d == 0) {
                res += d;
                n /= d;
            }
        }
        return res;
    }
}
```

