traces.inference_trace:
Count how often each character appears, then check that every nonzero count is the same.

The examples show a trailing space in the input (`"abacbc "`), probably a formatting artifact. The constraints say the string is only lowercase letters, so I count over a 256-sized array to handle any character safely. If a trailing space were really part of the input, it would be counted as a character with frequency 1 and break example 1. Since the constraints rule that out, I treat the input as lowercase letters only.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public bool AreOccurrencesEqual(string s) {
        int[] c = new int[256];
        foreach (char ch in s) c[ch & 255]++;
        int f = 0;
        foreach (int x in c) {
            if (x == 0) continue;
            if (f == 0) f = x;
            else if (f != x) return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

