Use the cross product of each point's offset from the first point against the direction from the first point to the second. If any cross product is nonzero, the points are not collinear. This avoids division, so vertical lines need no special case. Values stay within about 2·10^4 per difference, so products reach about 4·10^8 and fit in an int.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public bool CheckStraightLine(int[][] coordinates) {
        int x0 = coordinates[0][0], y0 = coordinates[0][1];
        int dx = coordinates[1][0] - x0, dy = coordinates[1][1] - y0;
        for (int i = 2; i < coordinates.Length; i++) {
            long ex = coordinates[i][0] - x0, ey = coordinates[i][1] - y0;
            if ((long)dx * ey - (long)dy * ex != 0) return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

