The maximum OR is the OR of all elements, since OR never loses bits. With at most 16 elements, a DFS over include/exclude choices visits at most 2^16 subsets, which is fast enough.

The recursion tracks the current OR. At the end of the array, it counts 1 if the current OR equals the maximum. The empty subset has OR 0, and the maximum is at least 1 because every `nums[i] >= 1`, so the empty subset is never counted.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    int target;
    int[] a;
    public int CountMaxOrSubsets(int[] nums) {
        a = nums;
        target = 0;
        foreach (int x in nums) target |= x;
        return Dfs(0, 0);
    }
    int Dfs(int i, int cur) {
        if (i == a.Length) return cur == target ? 1 : 0;
        return Dfs(i + 1, cur) + Dfs(i + 1, cur | a[i]);
    }
}
```

