traces.inference_trace:
This is a bitmask DP over which elements have been used. The number of operations already performed is popcount(mask)/2, so the next operation has index popcount(mask)/2 + 1.

1. Precompute `gcd[i][j]` for every pair of elements.
2. Let `dp[mask]` be the maximum score obtainable from the state where `mask` marks the removed elements. Process masks in increasing order and skip any mask with an odd popcount.
3. For a valid mask, let `k = popcount/2 + 1`. Find the first unused index `i`, then try every unused `j > i`. Always pairing the lowest unused element covers every pairing, because that element must be paired with something. Update `dp[mask | 1<<i | 1<<j] = max(dp[...], dp[mask] + k * gcd[i][j])`.
4. The answer is `dp[(1<<m) - 1]`, where `m = 2n`.

Fixing `i` as the lowest unused element is safe because the order of operations is determined by the DP, not by the index order. Which pair is chosen at which step is still free: the transition from `mask` assigns the pair to step `k`, and every pair-to-step assignment is reachable by a different path through the masks. However, the lowest unused element is forced into the current step `k` here, which would restrict the assignment. So I iterate over all pairs `(i, j)` that are both unused instead. With 2^14 masks and at most 91 pairs each, that is about 1.5M operations, which is fine.

Unreachable states keep the value 0 for the "not reached" case, which is safe since all scores are positive and we take maxima starting from `dp[0] = 0`. Only even-popcount masks are processed, and every such mask is reachable.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    static int Gcd(int a, int b) {
        while (b != 0) { int t = a % b; a = b; b = t; }
        return a;
    }
    public int MaxScore(int[] nums) {
        int m = nums.Length;
        int[,] g = new int[m, m];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)
            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++)
                g[i, j] = Gcd(nums[i], nums[j]);
        int full = 1 << m;
        int[] dp = new int[full];
        for (int mask = 0; mask < full; mask++) {
            int pc = 0;
            int x = mask;
            while (x != 0) { pc++; x &= x - 1; }
            if ((pc & 1) == 1) continue;
            int k = pc / 2 + 1;
            for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
                if ((mask & (1 << i)) != 0) continue;
                for (int j = i + 1; j < m; j++) {
                    if ((mask & (1 << j)) != 0) continue;
                    int nm = mask | (1 << i) | (1 << j);
                    int v = dp[mask] + k * g[i, j];
                    if (v > dp[nm]) dp[nm] = v;
                }
            }
        }
        return dp[full - 1];
    }
}
```

