Approach: reverse the graph and run a topological sort (Kahn's algorithm) starting from the terminal nodes.

1. For each node, set its out-degree to `graph[i].Length`.
2. For every edge `i -> j`, add `i` to the reverse adjacency list of `j`.
3. Put all nodes with out-degree 0 into a queue.
4. Pop a node, mark it safe, and decrement the out-degree of each of its predecessors. Any predecessor that reaches out-degree 0 goes into the queue.
5. Collect the safe nodes in index order, which gives an ascending result.

```csharp
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution {
    public IList<int> EventualSafeNodes(int[][] graph) {
        int n = graph.Length;
        var rev = new List<int>[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) rev[i] = new List<int>();
        int[] outd = new int[n];
        var q = new Queue<int>();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            outd[i] = graph[i].Length;
            foreach (int j in graph[i]) rev[j].Add(i);
            if (outd[i] == 0) q.Enqueue(i);
        }
        bool[] safe = new bool[n];
        while (q.Count > 0) {
            int u = q.Dequeue();
            safe[u] = true;
            foreach (int p in rev[u]) {
                outd[p]--;
                if (outd[p] == 0) q.Enqueue(p);
            }
        }
        var res = new List<int>();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) if (safe[i]) res.Add(i);
        return res;
    }
}
```

traces.inference_trace:
Binary search on the running time T. A time T is feasible if the sum of min(battery, T) over all batteries is at least n*T. A battery can contribute at most T minutes, because it cannot run on two computers at once.

The upper bound is sum/n, which is at most about 1e14, so I use long throughout. The sum of min(b, T) is at most 1e5 * 1e9 = 1e14 and n*T is at most about 1e14, so neither overflows.

Binary search with lo = 0 and hi = sum/n:
- While lo < hi, set mid = (lo + hi + 1) / 2.
- If feasible(mid), set lo = mid. Otherwise set hi = mid - 1.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public long MaxRunTime(int n, int[] batteries) {
        long sum = 0;
        foreach (var b in batteries) sum += b;
        long lo = 0, hi = sum / n;
        while (lo < hi) {
            long mid = (lo + hi + 1) / 2;
            long s = 0;
            foreach (var b in batteries) s += Math.Min((long)b, mid);
            if (s >= mid * n) lo = mid;
            else hi = mid - 1;
        }
        return lo;
    }
}
```

