Approach: removing an initial node deletes it from the graph entirely, so only the clean (non-initial) nodes matter for the count.

1. Mark the initial nodes. Find connected components among the non-initial nodes only (initial nodes are skipped).
2. For each component, collect the set of distinct initial nodes adjacent to it.
3. If exactly one initial node touches a component, removing that node saves the whole component, so add the component's size to `save[node]`.
4. Pick the initial node with the largest `save`. On ties, pick the smallest index. If every save is 0, this returns the smallest-index initial node.

Implementation details:
- Label components with a DFS or BFS over non-initial nodes, using `comp[i]` and a size array.
- For each component, find the adjacent initial nodes by iterating over its nodes and checking neighbors that are initial. To keep it simple, for each initial node `u` and each non-initial `v` with `graph[u][v]==1`, record the component of `v` in a per-component set. Use an array `cnt[comp]` and `who[comp]`, and mark per `(u, comp)` pairs so duplicates aren't counted. Per-`u` handling: keep a `lastSeen[comp] = u` marker, and increment `cnt` only when `lastSeen != u`.
- Sort `initial` first so ties resolve to the smallest index naturally, or compare explicitly.

Complexity is O(n²).

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution {
    public int MinMalwareSpread(int[][] graph, int[] initial) {
        int n = graph.Length;
        bool[] isInit = new bool[n];
        foreach (int x in initial) isInit[x] = true;
        int[] comp = new int[n];
        Array.Fill(comp, -1);
        List<int> sizes = new List<int>();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (isInit[i] || comp[i] != -1) continue;
            int id = sizes.Count;
            int size = 0;
            Stack<int> st = new Stack<int>();
            st.Push(i);
            comp[i] = id;
            while (st.Count > 0) {
                int u = st.Pop();
                size++;
                for (int v = 0; v < n; v++) {
                    if (graph[u][v] == 1 && !isInit[v] && comp[v] == -1) {
                        comp[v] = id;
                        st.Push(v);
                    }
                }
            }
            sizes.Add(size);
        }
        int c = sizes.Count;
        int[] cnt = new int[c];
        int[] who = new int[c];
        int[] last = new int[c];
        Array.Fill(last, -1);
        foreach (int u in initial) {
            for (int v = 0; v < n; v++) {
                if (graph[u][v] == 1 && !isInit[v]) {
                    int k = comp[v];
                    if (last[k] != u) {
                        last[k] = u;
                        cnt[k]++;
                        who[k] = u;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        int[] save = new int[n];
        for (int k = 0; k < c; k++) {
            if (cnt[k] == 1) save[who[k]] += sizes[k];
        }
        int best = -1;
        foreach (int u in initial) {
            if (best == -1 || save[u] > save[best] || (save[u] == save[best] && u < best)) best = u;
        }
        return best;
    }
}
```

