Greedy approach: sort the numbers in descending order and take elements from the largest until the taken sum is strictly greater than the remaining sum. Taking the largest elements first gives the minimum count and the maximum total sum for that count.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;

public class Solution {
    public IList<int> MinSubsequence(int[] nums) {
        int total = nums.Sum();
        var sorted = nums.OrderByDescending(x => x).ToArray();
        var res = new List<int>();
        int cur = 0;
        foreach (var x in sorted) {
            res.Add(x);
            cur += x;
            if (cur > total - cur) break;
        }
        return res;
    }
}
```

