Approach: put all points in a hash set. For each pair of points (i, j) with x1 != x2 and y1 != y2, treat them as opposite diagonal corners and check whether the other two corners, (x1, y2) and (x2, y1), are in the set. If they are, update the minimum area. With n ≤ 500 this is about 125k pairs, which is fast enough.

Each point is encoded as the long key x * 40001 + y, so the set is a `HashSet<long>`.

The area is at most 4e4 * 4e4 = 1.6e9, which fits in an int only up to 2.147e9, so I compute it as a long to be safe and convert at the end.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution {
    public int MinAreaRect(int[][] points) {
        var set = new HashSet<long>();
        foreach (var p in points) set.Add((long)p[0] * 40001 + p[1]);
        long best = long.MaxValue;
        int n = points.Length;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
                int x1 = points[i][0], y1 = points[i][1];
                int x2 = points[j][0], y2 = points[j][1];
                if (x1 == x2 || y1 == y2) continue;
                long area = Math.Abs((long)(x1 - x2)) * Math.Abs((long)(y1 - y2));
                if (area >= best) continue;
                if (set.Contains((long)x1 * 40001 + y2) && set.Contains((long)x2 * 40001 + y1)) {
                    best = area;
                }
            }
        }
        return best == long.MaxValue ? 0 : (int)best;
    }
}
```

