traces.inference_trace:
Convert each date to a day count since 1971-01-01, then return the absolute difference.

For a date (y, m, d), the day count is the sum of these parts:
- the days in all full years from 1971 up to y-1 (366 for a leap year, 365 otherwise),
- the days in the full months before month m of year y (using 29 for February in a leap year),
- the day of the month d.

A year is a leap year if it is divisible by 4 and not by 100, or divisible by 400. Within 1971–2100 this check gives the correct answer for 2000 (leap) and 2100 (not leap).

```csharp
using System;

public class Solution {
    private static bool Leap(int y) {
        return (y % 4 == 0 && y % 100 != 0) || y % 400 == 0;
    }

    private static int Count(string s) {
        var p = s.Split('-');
        int y = int.Parse(p[0]);
        int m = int.Parse(p[1]);
        int d = int.Parse(p[2]);
        int[] md = { 31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31 };
        int total = 0;
        for (int i = 1971; i < y; i++) {
            total += Leap(i) ? 366 : 365;
        }
        for (int i = 1; i < m; i++) {
            total += md[i - 1];
            if (i == 2 && Leap(y)) total++;
        }
        return total + d;
    }

    public int DaysBetweenDates(string date1, string date2) {
        return Math.Abs(Count(date1) - Count(date2));
    }
}
```

