For each rectangle, the largest square has side `min(l, w)`. I keep a running maximum of these sides and a count of how many rectangles reach it. When a larger side appears, I reset the count to 1; when the side equals the current maximum, I increment the count.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int CountGoodRectangles(int[][] rectangles) {
        int max = 0, count = 0;
        foreach (var r in rectangles) {
            int m = System.Math.Min(r[0], r[1]);
            if (m > max) {
                max = m;
                count = 1;
            } else if (m == max) {
                count++;
            }
        }
        return count;
    }
}
```

