traces.inference_trace:
Use a union-find structure. For each request, find the roots of u and v. If the roots are equal, the request succeeds. Otherwise, check every restriction (x, y): if the roots of x and y are exactly the roots of u and v (in either order), the request fails. If no restriction blocks it, union the two components and mark the request successful.

Each request costs O(restrictions) finds, so the total is about 10^6 operations times a near-constant find cost, which is fast enough.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    int[] p;
    int Find(int x) {
        while (p[x] != x) {
            p[x] = p[p[x]];
            x = p[x];
        }
        return x;
    }
    public bool[] FriendRequests(int n, int[][] restrictions, int[][] requests) {
        p = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) p[i] = i;
        var res = new bool[requests.Length];
        for (int j = 0; j < requests.Length; j++) {
            int a = Find(requests[j][0]);
            int b = Find(requests[j][1]);
            if (a == b) {
                res[j] = true;
                continue;
            }
            bool ok = true;
            foreach (var r in restrictions) {
                int x = Find(r[0]);
                int y = Find(r[1]);
                if ((x == a && y == b) || (x == b && y == a)) {
                    ok = false;
                    break;
                }
            }
            if (ok) {
                p[a] = b;
                res[j] = true;
            }
        }
        return res;
    }
}
```

