Use a monotonic stack of indices and iterate over the array twice (indices 0 to 2n-1, taking each index mod n).

For each position i, while the stack is non-empty and the value at the top index is less than `nums[i % n]`, pop that index and set its answer to `nums[i % n]`. Only push the index during the first pass (i < n). Any index left on the stack at the end keeps the default answer of -1.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int[] NextGreaterElements(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.Length;
        int[] res = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) res[i] = -1;
        var st = new System.Collections.Generic.Stack<int>();
        for (int i = 0; i < 2 * n; i++) {
            int v = nums[i % n];
            while (st.Count > 0 && nums[st.Peek()] < v) {
                res[st.Pop()] = v;
            }
            if (i < n) st.Push(i);
        }
        return res;
    }
}
```

