The approach is to count the minimum number of left and right parentheses to remove, then use DFS with deduplication.

1. Scan the string once. For each `(`, increment `open`. For each `)`, if `open > 0`, decrement `open`; otherwise increment `close`. At the end, `open` is the number of `(` to remove and `close` is the number of `)` to remove.

2. Run a DFS over the string that tracks the index, the current balance, the remaining removals `l` and `r`, and the built string (a `StringBuilder`).

3. At each character:
   - If it is `(`, either remove it (when `l > 0`) or keep it (balance + 1).
   - If it is `)`, either remove it (when `r > 0`) or keep it (only if balance > 0, then balance − 1).
   - If it is a letter, keep it.

4. At the end of the string, accept the result if `l == 0`, `r == 0` and balance is 0. Collect results in a `HashSet` to remove duplicates.

5. Pruning: the search never goes below zero balance, and the remaining-removal counters cannot go negative. Skipping duplicates is handled by the set. With at most 20 parentheses, the 2^20 worst case is acceptable.

6. Accepting when `l == 0 && r == 0` and balance is 0 is enough, since the total removals equal the minimum.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    HashSet<string> res = new HashSet<string>();
    string str;
    public IList<string> RemoveInvalidParentheses(string s) {
        str = s;
        int open = 0, close = 0;
        foreach (char c in s) {
            if (c == '(') open++;
            else if (c == ')') {
                if (open > 0) open--;
                else close++;
            }
        }
        Dfs(0, 0, open, close, new System.Text.StringBuilder());
        return new List<string>(res);
    }

    void Dfs(int i, int bal, int l, int r, System.Text.StringBuilder sb) {
        if (i == str.Length) {
            if (l == 0 && r == 0 && bal == 0) res.Add(sb.ToString());
            return;
        }
        char c = str[i];
        if (c == '(') {
            if (l > 0) Dfs(i + 1, bal, l - 1, r, sb);
            sb.Append(c);
            Dfs(i + 1, bal + 1, l, r, sb);
            sb.Length--;
        } else if (c == ')') {
            if (r > 0) Dfs(i + 1, bal, l, r - 1, sb);
            if (bal > 0) {
                sb.Append(c);
                Dfs(i + 1, bal - 1, l, r, sb);
                sb.Length--;
            }
        } else {
            sb.Append(c);
            Dfs(i + 1, bal, l, r, sb);
            sb.Length--;
        }
    }
}
```

