traces.inference_trace:
Approach: split each cell into 4 triangles (0 = top, 1 = right, 2 = bottom, 3 = left) and merge them with union-find.

- Inside a cell, a blank space unions all four triangles. A `/` unions top with left (0 and 3) and bottom with right (2 and 1). A `\` unions top with right (0 and 1) and bottom with left (2 and 3).
- Across cells, the bottom triangle of (i,j) unions with the top triangle of (i+1,j), and the right triangle of (i,j) unions with the left triangle of (i,j+1).
- The answer is the number of distinct components.

The index of a triangle is (i*n+j)*4+k.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    int[] p;
    int Find(int x) {
        while (p[x] != x) {
            p[x] = p[p[x]];
            x = p[x];
        }
        return x;
    }
    void Union(int a, int b) {
        a = Find(a);
        b = Find(b);
        if (a != b) p[a] = b;
    }
    public int RegionsBySlashes(string[] grid) {
        int n = grid.Length;
        p = new int[n * n * 4];
        for (int i = 0; i < p.Length; i++) p[i] = i;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                int b = (i * n + j) * 4;
                char c = grid[i][j];
                if (c == ' ') {
                    Union(b, b + 1);
                    Union(b, b + 2);
                    Union(b, b + 3);
                } else if (c == '/') {
                    Union(b, b + 3);
                    Union(b + 1, b + 2);
                } else {
                    Union(b, b + 1);
                    Union(b + 2, b + 3);
                }
                if (i + 1 < n) Union(b + 2, ((i + 1) * n + j) * 4);
                if (j + 1 < n) Union(b + 1, (i * n + j + 1) * 4 + 3);
            }
        }
        int count = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < p.Length; i++) if (Find(i) == i) count++;
        return count;
    }
}
```

