traces.inference_trace:
Since values are at most 50, I keep, for each value, a stack of the (node, depth) pairs currently on the root-to-node path. For a node, I check all 50 values that are coprime with its value and take the deepest top-of-stack entry.

Recursion could overflow the stack for n = 1e5, so the DFS is iterative.

Iterative DFS design:
- Build adjacency lists.
- Keep arrays `parent`, `depth`, an edge-iterator index `it[node]`, and `stacks[v]` as a `List<int>` of nodes per value.
- Precompute `coprime[v]`, the list of values in 1..50 coprime with v.
- On entering a node u:
  - Compute `ans[u]` as the node with maximum depth among `stacks[w].Last` for w in `coprime[nums[u]]`, or -1 if none.
  - Push u onto `stacks[nums[u]]`.
- Then iterate over the neighbours of u, skipping the parent. For each child, set its depth and parent and enter it.
- When the neighbours are exhausted, pop u from `stacks[nums[u]]` and pop it from the DFS stack.

The ancestor check is correct because u is pushed only after its answer is computed, so it never counts as its own ancestor. Entries in the value stacks are exactly the current path, since each node is popped on exit.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution {
    static int Gcd(int a, int b) {
        while (b != 0) { int t = a % b; a = b; b = t; }
        return a;
    }
    public int[] GetCoprimes(int[] nums, int[][] edges) {
        int n = nums.Length;
        var adj = new List<int>[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) adj[i] = new List<int>();
        foreach (var e in edges) {
            adj[e[0]].Add(e[1]);
            adj[e[1]].Add(e[0]);
        }
        var cop = new List<int>[51];
        for (int v = 1; v <= 50; v++) {
            cop[v] = new List<int>();
            for (int w = 1; w <= 50; w++)
                if (Gcd(v, w) == 1) cop[v].Add(w);
        }
        var stacks = new List<int>[51];
        for (int v = 0; v <= 50; v++) stacks[v] = new List<int>();
        int[] ans = new int[n];
        int[] parent = new int[n];
        int[] depth = new int[n];
        int[] it = new int[n];
        var st = new Stack<int>();
        parent[0] = -1;
        depth[0] = 0;
        // enter root
        ans[0] = -1;
        stacks[nums[0]].Add(0);
        st.Push(0);
        while (st.Count > 0) {
            int u = st.Peek();
            if (it[u] < adj[u].Count) {
                int c = adj[u][it[u]++];
                if (c == parent[u]) continue;
                parent[c] = u;
                depth[c] = depth[u] + 1;
                int best = -1;
                foreach (int w in cop[nums[c]]) {
                    var s = stacks[w];
                    if (s.Count > 0) {
                        int x = s[s.Count - 1];
                        if (best == -1 || depth[x] > depth[best]) best = x;
                    }
                }
                ans[c] = best;
                stacks[nums[c]].Add(c);
                st.Push(c);
            } else {
                var s = stacks[nums[u]];
                s.RemoveAt(s.Count - 1);
                st.Pop();
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
```

