traces.inference_trace:
Count the soldiers in each row, sort the row indices by (count, index), and return the first k.

Since the matrix is at most 100×100, a plain count and sort is fast enough. I use a stable key by comparing the count first and the index second, which avoids relying on the sort being stable.

```csharp
using System;

public class Solution {
    public int[] KWeakestRows(int[][] mat, int k) {
        int m = mat.Length;
        int[] cnt = new int[m];
        int[] idx = new int[m];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            int c = 0;
            foreach (int v in mat[i]) c += v;
            cnt[i] = c;
            idx[i] = i;
        }
        Array.Sort(idx, (a, b) => cnt[a] != cnt[b] ? cnt[a].CompareTo(cnt[b]) : a.CompareTo(b));
        int[] res = new int[k];
        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) res[i] = idx[i];
        return res;
    }
}
```

