traces.inference_trace:
The approach is to turn the equation into one weighted sum and search over digit assignments.

Each letter gets a coefficient: for every letter in a word, add 10^position (position counted from the right), and for letters in the result, subtract 10^position. The equation holds exactly when the sum of coefficient × digit over all letters equals 0.

Letters that appear first in a word or in the result (when its length is greater than 1) cannot be 0. The input strings may contain trailing spaces, as in the examples, so I trim them first.

Then a backtracking search assigns distinct digits to the at most 10 letters and checks whether the sum reaches 0. That is at most 10! ≈ 3.6M leaves, which is fast enough.

Steps:
1. Build `coef[26]` and `nonzero[26]`.
2. Collect the letters that are present.
3. Run `dfs(idx, sum)`. At the end, return `sum == 0`. Otherwise try each unused digit, skipping 0 when the letter is flagged nonzero.

A single-letter word may be 0, so the leading-zero rule applies only when the length is greater than 1.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    long[] coef = new long[26];
    bool[] nz = new bool[26];
    int[] letters;
    bool[] used = new bool[10];

    public bool IsSolvable(string[] words, string result) {
        bool[] present = new bool[26];
        foreach (var w0 in words) {
            string w = w0.Trim();
            long p = 1;
            for (int i = w.Length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
                int c = w[i] - 'A';
                coef[c] += p;
                p *= 10;
                present[c] = true;
            }
            if (w.Length > 1) nz[w[0] - 'A'] = true;
        }
        string r = result.Trim();
        {
            long p = 1;
            for (int i = r.Length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
                int c = r[i] - 'A';
                coef[c] -= p;
                p *= 10;
                present[c] = true;
            }
            if (r.Length > 1) nz[r[0] - 'A'] = true;
        }
        var list = new System.Collections.Generic.List<int>();
        for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) if (present[i]) list.Add(i);
        letters = list.ToArray();
        return Dfs(0, 0);
    }

    bool Dfs(int idx, long sum) {
        if (idx == letters.Length) return sum == 0;
        int c = letters[idx];
        for (int d = 0; d < 10; d++) {
            if (used[d]) continue;
            if (d == 0 && nz[c]) continue;
            used[d] = true;
            if (Dfs(idx + 1, sum + coef[c] * d)) { used[d] = false; return true; }
            used[d] = false;
        }
        return false;
    }
}
```

